    "source": "UN Trade and Development (UNCTAD), distributed in World Development Indicators.",
    "measure": "Indices of merchandise volume, current US dollar value, and unit value, published with 2015 as the reference year. The unit-value measure can reflect changes in the mix of goods as well as prices. The volume index adjusts for unit-value changes.",
    "interpretation": "Each series measures change within an economy. Cross-country index levels do not measure relative trade size. The explorer uses all three source indices independently. Their rounded values need not reproduce each other by multiplication.",
    "coverage": "Volume and value run from 2005 to 2024 in this edition. Unit value runs from 1980 to 2025. Missing components stay unavailable. Tuvalu’s own 2015 unit-value entries differ from 100 and remain as published."
  },
